From: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 10:44:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 54/71] docs: Record the notification, lock-screen sound and
 elevator retract fixes

The notification sound was inaudible because the speaker ring/notification
volume sat at 3/15 (track gain 0.063, about -24 dB); a second failure mode
kills all sound after long use, when the HAL's awinic VI feedback fails to
start and leaks iv_feedback_count, so the speaker route is never re-enabled
again until a reboot.

The keyguard sound comes from the lock_sound / unlock_sound settings, which
were empty and fell back to an android R.raw.lock that this framework-res
does not contain; point them at the product partition's Lock.ogg/Unlock.ogg.

The camera retract stopped a few millimetres short because the driver drives
the down stroke with the same open-loop time as the raise and the factory
compensates with its hall retry, which is dead here.  Raising the calibrated
travel time (cali_time 2790 -> 3630) through the hall core's SET_CALI ioctl
fixes it without touching the kernel.

Signed-off-by: Zhiyu722 <Zhiyu722@users.noreply.github.com>
